- add OS detection to setup.sh from Ansible's bootstrap.sh

- consider using github.com/filosottile/mkcert for generating and installing certificates along with nss

- if not wanting to use mkcert, add support for MacOS to setup.sh the old fashioned way
    - programmatically add CA cert to MacOS keychain
    ```
    # Import the CA certificate to the System keychain
    sudo security add-trusted-cert -d -r trustRoot -k /Library/Keychains/System.keychain /path/to/ca.crt
    ```
    - programmatically import certs to Firefox
    ```
    # get certutil from nss package
    brew install nss
    # get firefox profile dir
    FIREFOX_PROFILE_DIR=$(find $HOME/Library/Application\ Support/Firefox/Profiles -name "*.default-release")
    # import CA cert
    certutil -A -n "My CA" -t "CT,c,c" -i /path/to/ca.crt -d sql:"$FIREFOX_PROFILE_DIR"
    # import wildcard cert
    certutil -A -n "*.lab.test" -t "P,p,p" -i /path/to/wildcard.lab.test.crt -d sql:"$FIREFOX_PROFILE_DIR"
    ```

